---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Header } from "../components/Header";
import { publications, profile } from "../data/profile";

const pub = publications.find((p) => p.id === "bhutani2026photoelasticity")!;
const authors = [
    { name: "Namit Bhutani", sup: "1", url: "/" },
    { name: "Tathagata Ray", sup: "1" },
    { name: "Sumanta Pattanaik", sup: "2" },
];
const links = pub.links.filter((l) => l.label !== "Project page");

const results = [
    { big: "> 120 FPS", label: "full pipeline at 1920×1080 on a laptop RTX 3070" },
    { big: "8.55×", label: "faster than the deterministic 16-wavelength loop on the same GPU and grid" },
    { big: "2.28 ms", label: "per frame for the 128³ FEM volume: fits a 90 Hz VR frame (11.1 ms)" },
    { big: "0.4%", label: "fringe-order error vs. the exact beam solution at the neutral axis" },
];
---

<Layout
    title="Real-Time Spectral Photoelasticity | Pacific Graphics 2026"
    description="Real-time spectral photoelasticity via stochastic hero-wavelength ray marching and stress-aware temporal reprojection. Pacific Graphics 2026."
    image="/og.jpg"
>
    <Header client:load />
    <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-10 md:py-14">
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Pacific Graphics 2026 · Conference Papers</p>
        <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight leading-tight">
            Real-Time Spectral Photoelasticity
            <span class="block mt-1 text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-muted-foreground">
                via Stochastic Hero-Wavelength Ray Marching and Stress-Aware Temporal Reprojection
            </span>
        </h1>

        <p class="mt-5 text-base">
            {authors.map((a, i) => (
                <>
                    {a.url ? <a href={a.url} class="font-semibold text-primary hover:underline">{a.name}</a> : <span>{a.name}</span>}
                    <sup>{a.sup}</sup>{i < authors.length - 1 ? ", " : ""}
                </>
            ))}
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
            <sup>1</sup> BITS Pilani – Hyderabad Campus, India &nbsp; <sup>2</sup> University of Central Florida, USA
        </p>

        <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            {links.map((l) => (
                <a
                    href={l.href}
                    target={l.href.startsWith("http") ? "_blank" : undefined}
                    rel={l.href.startsWith("http") ? "noopener noreferrer" : undefined}
                    class="font-mono text-sm px-3 py-1.5 bg-foreground text-background hover:bg-foreground/85 transition-colors"
                >
                    {l.label}
                </a>
            ))}
            <a href="#bibtex" class="font-mono text-sm px-3 py-1.5 ring-1 ring-foreground/20 hover:ring-primary hover:text-primary">BibTeX</a>
        </div>

        <figure class="mt-8">
            <video
                src="/media/pg26-load-demo.mp4"
                poster="/media/pg26-load-demo.jpg"
                autoplay
                muted
                loop
                playsinline
                class="w-full ring-1 ring-foreground/10 bg-black"
            ></video>
            <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
                Live in NVIDIA Falcor: dragging the load along an acrylic beam between crossed polarisers.
                The stress field and the coloured isochromatic fringes update every frame.
            </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <section class="mt-10">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">TL;DR</h2>
            <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">{pub.summary}</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-10">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Abstract</h2>
            <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-[15px]">
                We address rendering photoelastic stress fringes at real-time rates. The state-of-the-art
                method, Büssler et al.'s GPU raycaster, integrates the Jones Calculus along each ray for 16
                fixed wavelengths, giving frame times of 231 to 6,400 ms and no interactive stress updates.
                Adapting Hero Wavelength Sampling to this integral with four SIMD-vectorised wavelengths rather
                than a deterministic 16-step loop yields an unbiased estimator with a theoretical 4× wavelength
                reduction.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-[15px]">
                Interactivity introduces a critical temporal challenge: fringe patterns shift instantaneously
                under dynamic loads while geometry remains static. This violates the geometric motion assumptions
                of standard temporal anti-aliasing (TAA), causing severe persistent ghosting. We resolve it with a
                stress-aware history rejection gate driven by the temporal gradient of the local principal stress
                difference. To isolate our algorithmic gains from simulation constraints, we evaluate on two
                interactive analytical stress fields and one pre-computed FEM tensor volume (the Kirsch plate),
                matching prior offline methods' data setup. The framework achieves over 120 FPS at 1080p on
                consumer hardware, an 8.55× algorithmic speedup over the deterministic baseline on identical
                hardware, and over 100× absolute improvement against the prior published state of the art.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-10">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Results</h2>
            <div class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
                {results.map((r) => (
                    <div class="p-4 bg-card ring-1 ring-foreground/10">
                        <div class="font-mono text-3xl text-primary">{r.big}</div>
                        <div class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">{r.label}</div>
                    </div>
                ))}
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-10">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">No ghosting when the load moves</h2>
            <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
                The beam never moves, so motion vectors are zero and standard TAA keeps stale fringes for 25–28
                frames. Our gate keeps one stress value per pixel and drops history only where it changed.
                Top: standard TAA. Bottom: our stress-aware gate.
            </p>
            <video
                src="/media/pg26-taa-compare.mp4"
                poster="/media/pg26-taa-compare.jpg"
                autoplay
                muted
                loop
                playsinline
                class="mt-4 w-full max-w-2xl ring-1 ring-foreground/10 bg-black"
            ></video>
        </section>

        <section id="bibtex" class="mt-10">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">BibTeX</h2>
            <pre class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto text-xs leading-relaxed p-4 bg-muted font-mono">{pub.bibtex}</pre>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-10 p-6 bg-muted">
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
                I'm applying to research master's and PhD programs for 2027.
                Questions about this work, or about my application?
                <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`} class="text-primary font-semibold underline underline-offset-4">{profile.email}</a>
            </p>
        </section>

        <p class="mt-10 text-sm"><a href="/" class="text-primary hover:underline">← Namit Bhutani</a></p>
    </main>
</Layout>
